id=a52sxq_kernel_feature_check
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: kernel compatibility check
author=kusti420
description=This ROM expects the bone-machine 5.4.302 kernel with the k4 patches (kernel_bone_machine); users who flash another kernel lose features silently or bootloop. Adds /system/bin/k4-kernel-diag (adb shell k4-kernel-diag [-v]): one line, "kernel OK (bone-machine 5.4.302 k4 caps ringbuf btf uvc8 pt su gpu)" or "kernel MISSING: <feature> (<what breaks>), ..." plus the kernel it found, what merely differs from k4 and what it could not check. Probes are read-only and cheap (uname, /proc/version, one fixed-string pass over /proc/kallsyms, /proc/config.gz if present, /proc/cgroups, cap_last_cap, sysfs/configfs nodes and usb_f_uvc module parameters); a probe it cannot read reports "not checked", never MISSING. Critical: BPF ring buffer maps (k4 0006; our a52_netd.o pins ringbuf maps, without them bpfloader reboot-loops / system_server aborts), cgroup v1 cpuset cpu cpuacct blkio memory freezer. Feature: BTF (0005, per-app CPU time), UVC gadget + format enumeration (0009, Webcam, only counted when ro.usb.uvc.enabled=true), battery pass_through (0008, only when the floating feature enables it), pd_disable. Minor: caps 38-40 (0001; zygote_next_kernel54 clamps), KernelSU, close_range, UVC stream params (0012, 0015/0016 = uvc8), GPU NAP/undervolt/idle-timer reverts (0002-0004). Init runs it once after sys.boot_completed=1 (k4_kernel_check.rc): one line to logcat (tag K4KernelCheck, W when something is missing) and sys.k4.kernel.ok=1/0, sys.k4.kernel.missing, sys.k4.kernel.minor, sys.k4.kernel.id. Its SELinux domain k4kcheck (enforcing, plat_sepolicy.cil) only reads those nodes and sets system_prop; Samsung's init shell domain could not read them. Report only: ro.usb.uvc.enabled stays a build-time decision (usb_webcam), because init.qcom.usb.sh only runs at "on boot", after zygote-start, so a boot-time setprop would race UsbService; no notification either (cmd notification from a boot service needs binder rules into system_server). Test mode: K4KC_ROOT=<fake tree> k4-kernel-diag [--boot].
